            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0073" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.1012 Anti-War/74: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-21T12:00:00-04:00">April 21,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>68. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 37 of April 12, 5 p.m., and my
                    telegram No. 66 of April 15, noon.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d5-f1"/> The following
                    countries will sign the document of adhesion at a ceremony to be held here on or
                    before April 27: Bolivia, Ecuador, Guatemala, Panama, Paraguay, Venezuela. The
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs desires to know whether I shall receive
                    authorization to sign along with the other countries.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
